# Why this file exists on this branch and nowhere else.
#
# The live site is deployed by Vercel's Git integration, which uploads only
# committed files. A `vercel deploy` from a working copy uploads everything
# git does *not* ignore — and on this branch that is several hundred megabytes
# of local scratch work plus a broken symlink that fails the build outright:
#
#   Error: /vercel/path0/.scratch/demos/android/demosnitro is not a valid symlink
#
# That is the shape of every manual redeploy of the Archive. Nothing pushes to
# `old` — it is frozen, by definition (ADR-0009) — so a manual redeploy from a
# dirty checkout is the *only* way this host is ever rebuilt, and this file is
# what makes that work. It changes nothing about what is served.
#
# `.gitignore` already covers /public/demo/ and /public/thumbnails/, the local
# staging copies of Assets (ADR-0001). What it does not cover is the rest of
# what accumulates in a working copy.

# Effort records. Never served, and .scratch/demos/android/demosnitro is a
# symlink to a path that no longer exists.
/.scratch/

# Stray recordings and images at the repo root. A 486MB .mp4 here is a
# Staging copy that was never published.
/*.mp4
/*.png
/*.svg

# Build output and local tooling, for completeness. The Git integration never
# uploads these; a CLI deploy would.
/.next
/test-results
/playwright-report
/node_modules
